      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Up to date only 13 cases of left main coronary artery aneurysms have been reported in literature; of these, 8 were associated with atherosclerosis. This report details the case of a large aneurysm of left main coronary artery angiographically documented in 46-year old man with exertional angina pectoris and myocardial infarction."},
